    "result_text": "You can now say who a task is for, and their name shows in that task's row. I ran `bin/e2e` and the acceptance test passes.\n\nYour request mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app's server is Spring Boot (the package names say `officefloor`). I made the server changes in the existing Spring code.\n\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V54__task_assignee.sql`, adds an optional `assignee` column to the task table.\n- **Server:** tasks now store an optional assignee, limited to 255 characters. When a task is created, spaces around the name are trimmed and a blank name is saved as empty. The `/__test__/seed` endpoint also accepts `assignee` for tasks.\n- **Front end:** the add-task form has a new optional \"Assignee\" field (`data-testid=\"task-form-assignee\"`). The task table has a new \"Assignee\" column whose cells use `data-testid=\"task-assignee\"`, which is what the test checks. No existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.\n\nYou can only set the assignee when adding a task. There's no way to change it on an existing task yet.",
